    "question": {
      ":question/id": "0bade6c7-cd43-5d21-823b-4952e19f42d7",
      ":question/problem": "Find the antiderivative of\n$-\\frac{6}{\\sqrt[7]{x^{8}}}+\\frac{1}{x^{5}}+3x^{7}.$ For real $x\\ne 0$.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Using the sum and constant factor rules, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}& \\int\\left(-\\frac{6}{\\sqrt[7]{x^{8}}}+\\frac{1}{x^{5}}+3x^{7}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\ &= \\int\\left(-6x^{\\frac{-8}{7}}+x^{-5}+3x^{7}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\ &= -6\\int x^{\\frac{-8}{7}}\\,\\mathrm{d}x+\\int x^{-5}\\,\\mathrm{d}x+3\\int x^{7}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\ &= -6\\left(\\frac{x^{\\frac{-8}{7}+1}}{(\\frac{-8}{7}+1)}\\right)+\\left(\\frac{x^{-5+1}}{(-5+1)}\\right)\\\\ &\\quad +3\\left(\\frac{x^{7+1}}{(7+1)}\\right)+C\\\\ &= \\frac{42}{\\sqrt[7]{x}}-\\frac{1}{4x^{4}}+\\frac{3x^{8}}{8}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
