      ":question/problem": "Find the antiderivative of\n$2x^{5}+\\frac{1}{x^{4}}-\\frac{6}{\\sqrt[7]{x^{8}}}.$ For real $x\\ne 0$.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Using the sum and constant factor rules, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}& \\int\\left(2x^{5}+\\frac{1}{x^{4}}-\\frac{6}{\\sqrt[7]{x^{8}}}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\ &= \\int\\left(2x^{5}+x^{-4}-6x^{\\frac{-8}{7}}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\ &= 2\\int x^{5}\\,\\mathrm{d}x+\\int x^{-4}\\,\\mathrm{d}x-6\\int x^{\\frac{-8}{7}}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\ &= 2\\left(\\frac{x^{5+1}}{(5+1)}\\right)+\\left(\\frac{x^{-4+1}}{(-4+1)}\\right)\\\\ &\\quad -6\\left(\\frac{x^{\\frac{-8}{7}+1}}{(\\frac{-8}{7}+1)}\\right)+C\\\\ &= \\frac{x^{6}}{3}-\\frac{1}{3x^{3}}+\\frac{42}{\\sqrt[7]{x}}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
