      ":question/problem": "Find the antiderivative of\n$\\frac{6}{x^{2}}+6x^{3}+4\\sqrt[3]{x^{2}}.$ For real $x\\ne 0$.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Using the sum and constant factor rules, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}& \\int\\left(\\frac{6}{x^{2}}+6x^{3}+4\\sqrt[3]{x^{2}}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\ &= \\int\\left(6x^{-2}+6x^{3}+4x^{\\frac{2}{3}}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\ &= 6\\int x^{-2}\\,\\mathrm{d}x+6\\int x^{3}\\,\\mathrm{d}x+4\\int x^{\\frac{2}{3}}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\ &= 6\\left(\\frac{x^{-2+1}}{(-2+1)}\\right)+6\\left(\\frac{x^{3+1}}{(3+1)}\\right)\\\\ &\\quad +4\\left(\\frac{x^{\\frac{2}{3}+1}}{(\\frac{2}{3}+1)}\\right)+C\\\\ &= -\\frac{6}{x}+\\frac{3x^{4}}{2}+\\frac{12\\sqrt[3]{x^{5}}}{5}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
